poems.text:
Only a baby small,
    Dropped from the skies,
Only a laughing face,
    Two sunny eyes;
Only two cherry lips,
    One chubby nose;
Only two little hands,
    Ten little toes.

Only a golden head,
    Curly and soft;
Only a tongue that wags
    Loudly and oft;
Only a little brain,
    Empty of thought;
Only a little heart,
    Troubled with naught.

Only a tender flower
    Sent us to rear;
Only a life to love
    While we are here;
Only a baby small,
    Never at rest;
Small, but how dear to us,
    God knoweth best.
